   "name": "Compile the slide's whole run to JavaScript, each livelit's model a parameter",
   "what": "hazel-jit compiles the slide's elaborated program once into a JavaScript function whose parameters are the livelits' models. A slider's event calls it with the new model, and every livelit draws from its answers at the page's next redraw, before the worker has answered.",
   "measured": "A step's picture 1.33 to 1.71 s on build 3, 208 to 236 ms on build 5 (steps 2 to 4; report 049). In Node, a slider's step 684 ms on the interpreter, 2.3 to 2.5 ms compiled (report 045).",
   "today": "It is why a step shows in about 20 ms: the run answers in 2 to 3 ms (5 to 12 for a step's first event).",
